# DianaSh golden corpus. Recorded from the C# shell, byte for byte, and frozen since its recorder went with the C# core host on 2026-11-07 - see EmuSen_DianaSh.md §13.4.
# Patterns: <ROOT> is the sandbox's real root, <TEMP> the corpus's real temporary folder, <INSTALL> the install's real directory;
# a 'match' block is a regular expression the whole output must match, written where a line prints a time or a measured number.
command watch
usage 1   watch add <space> <addr> <len> [write|read|both]
usage 2                                 register a watch, prints matching accesses live + stores them
usage 3                                 (default write, matching this command's original behavior)
usage 4   watch list                    list active watches with their IDs and access kind
usage 5   watch log <id> [<count>]      show a watch's recorded events (default 20)
usage 6   watch summary <id>            group a watch's recorded events by access site (Context),
usage 7                                 showing each unique site once with a hit count instead of
usage 8                                 every individual event - the dynamic, addressing-mode-agnostic
usage 9                                 equivalent of `readers`/`writers`, which only find statically-
usage 10                                 visible absolute/absolute-long instructions and miss indexed/
usage 11                                 indirect access entirely. Only covers whatever's still in the
usage 12                                 watch's own bounded event buffer, same as `watch log`.
usage 13   watch clear <id>              clear a watch's stored events (doesn't remove the watch)
usage 14   watch remove <id>             remove a watch entirely

case with no target
target none
covers 1
$ watch list
out 65
Error: No ROM loaded - this command needs an active debug target.
status 1
action none
end

